  "notes": "Rules of thumb (35% of gross pay on the car; 20/4/10: 20% down, 4-year loan, total car costs ≤ 10% of gross monthly pay). 60,000 × 0.35 = 21,000. 21,000 × 0.20 = 4,200; 21,000 − 4,200 = 16,800 borrowed. Payment factor at 7% APR over 48 months = r / (1 − (1 + r)^−48) with r = 0.07/12 → 0.023946 ≈ 0.024; 16,800 × 0.024 = 403.20 → ≈ $403 (exact amortised payment $402.30). 60,000 ÷ 12 × 0.10 = 500. 500 − 403 = 97 → ≈ $97 (exact 97.70)."
